\DOC EXISTS_E2_TAC

\TYPE {EXISTS_E2_TAC : term list ref -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes a goal equating an explicit event-list expression with {APPEND u e},
where {u} is an undetermined list variable, by choosing a witness for it and
discharging the equation.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {allowed_vars_e : term list ref} is a mutable reference holding
the list of terms — typically program-level variables such as pointers, program
counters and loop indices — that are permitted to occur in the witness chosen
for the unknown list variable {u}. The tactic applies to a goal whose
conclusion is {t = APPEND u e}, where {t} is a concrete list expression built
from {CONS}, list literals and {APPEND} over a trailing tail {e}, and {u} is
the yet-undetermined list variable; in all observed traces the right-hand side
is an {APPEND} of a single variable onto the same trailing tail {e} that occurs
at the end of {t}. The assumptions {A} are left unused and unchanged, and vary
widely across the traces without playing any visible role.
{
   A ?- t = APPEND u e
   ========================  EXISTS_E2_TAC allowed_vars_e
}

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this closing behaviour, and only conclusions of
exactly this shape.

\ENDDOC
